# Obsidian notes

The `notes/` folder is an Obsidian vault exposed through the `obsidian` MCP server (vault id `notes`).
It holds the user's tasks, page ideas, client feedback and project knowledge.

## Before starting a task
- For any code change, first search `Code map.md` for the page/feature name and open only the files
  it lists. Fall back to searching the code only if the map has no entry.
- Search the vault with `obsidian_search_vault` (vault `notes`) using 1–3 keywords from the request,
  e.g. the page name, feature, or "deploy". Read only the notes that match with `obsidian_read_note`.
- Do not read every note or list the whole vault. Skip the search for small talk or one-line questions.
- If a note conflicts with the user's message, follow the message and mention the conflict.
- `Project overview.md` has the repo layout, local ports and the Netlify deploy command.

## After finishing a task
- If a note listed the task (e.g. a `- [ ]` item in a Todo note), tick it off with `obsidian_edit_note`.
- If you add, move, rename or delete a page, component, content file or API route,
  update `Code map.md` in the same task.
- When something durable changes (new page, new env var, deploy steps, design decisions),
  update `Project overview.md` or the relevant note. Keep edits short.
- Never write passwords, API keys, database URLs or anything from `LOCAL-LOGIN.txt` / `.env` into notes.
